{"id": "unknown-2026-05-29-007", "date": "2026-05-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 22, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["loss", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "ICE cotton snaps losing streak, supported by weaker dollar", "content": "ICE cotton futures rebounded yesterday, snapping a six-session losing streak as a weaker US dollar and strength in broader commodity markets supported prices.\nThe July 2026 contract settled 1.11 per cent higher at 76.77 cents per pound, though gains only partly recovered recent losses.\nRising certified stocks, bearish technical signals and cautious sentiment continued to weigh on the outlook.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-snaps-losing-streak-supported-by-weaker-dollar-310634-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-29-008", "date": "2026-05-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 22, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cambodia’s $32-bn green investment fund to cut GHG emissions by 2035", "content": "Cambodia’s Ministry of Environment has allocated over $32 billion to green investments over a 10-year period till 2035 to achieve specific targets to reduce greenhouse gas emissions by up to 55 per cent. \nMinister of Environment Eang Sophalleth told a recent workshop in Phnom Penh that there is a need to mobilise funds from external sources like committed developed countries to achieve this target. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/cambodia-s-32-bn-green-investment-fund-to-cut-ghg-emissions-by-2035-310630-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-29-009", "date": "2026-05-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 22, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["sustainable_textile"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["expand", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Resale booms, but circular fashion economics still do not work", "content": "The resale and repair economy is pushing governments to reduce VAT, sales tax and labour costs on secondhand fashion.\nResale demand is rising strongly, but sorting, repair and sustainable material costs remain margin pressures.\nWith EPR rules expanding, circular fashion is shifting from a sustainability narrative towards a policy-driven industrial system.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/resale-booms-but-circular-fashion-economics-still-do-not-work-310614-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-29-010", "date": "2026-05-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 22, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["record", "decline", "slow", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "China widens dominance in Israel apparel market despite slowdown", "content": "Israel’s apparel imports fell 12.15 per cent year-on-year to $671.3 million in Q1 2026, reflecting weaker sourcing demand.\nChina strengthened its dominance by increasing its market share to 55.55 per cent despite slightly lower shipments.\nBangladesh, Turkiye and India also recorded declines, while trousers and shorts remained the largest imported apparel category.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/china-widens-dominance-in-israel-apparel-market-despite-slowdown-310578-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
